Kind: ablation
Issue: #808
Takes out: the check in ipc_kmsg_get() that refuses a send size the trailer cannot follow -- the buffer is then sized by size + MAX_TRAILER_SIZE wrapped in 32 bits, a small buffer, and copyinmsg() copies the whole size into it, so act_test's arm 27 sends 0xFFFFFFFC bytes and the trap answers with something other than MACH_SEND_TOO_LARGE instead of refusing at once
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Expect: act_test: \[27\] a send of 0xFFFFFFFC bytes answered 0x[0-9a-f]+, not MACH_SEND_TOO_LARGE
Note: Judged under QEMU (TCG and KVM), act_test's arm 27, on victus 02/11/2026: the ablated tree caught 4 of 4 and the fixed tree passed 4 of 4.  On the fixed tree the trap refuses the size before any buffer, so the arm overruns nothing; the ablated tree wraps the sum, takes a small buffer and faults in copyinmsg, answering a code other than MACH_SEND_TOO_LARGE.

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_kmsg.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_kmsg.c
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_kmsg.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_kmsg.c
@@ -835,8 +835,6 @@
 	 * added to it: the sum below must be the size of the buffer that
 	 * copyinmsg() then fills with `size' bytes.
 	 */
-	if (size > MACH_MSG_SIZE_MAX - MAX_TRAILER_SIZE)
-		return MACH_SEND_TOO_LARGE;
 
 #if	MACH_RT
